1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:04,087
We'll bring back what we learned
to Travis Japan.

2
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:11,011
We'll embark on many, many more
spectacular journeys together. Agreed?

3
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,804
[all] Agreed!

4
00:00:12,888 --> 00:00:15,349
-[cheering, in English] Let's go, TJ!
-Let's go!

5
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:16,683
Let's go!

6
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:19,353
[in Japanese] Thank you!

7
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:22,940
Couldn't have asked for better band mates.
You're the best!

8
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:25,317
[narrator] It's the special summer break

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,652
Noel organized
for the Travis Japan members.

10
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:30,405
After traveling through
the southwestern United States,

11
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:32,574
the Travis Japan members
arrived in Sedona.

12
00:00:33,951 --> 00:00:36,662
The seven friends enjoyed
a heartfelt reunion.

13
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,747
[♪ opening theme music plays]

14
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:06,108
Travis Japan
SUMMER VACATION!! IN THE USA

15
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:12,155
Sedona, Arizona.

16
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:20,163
[Noel, in Japanese]
No matter how many years pass,

17
00:01:20,247 --> 00:01:22,040
Travis Japan will never forget this place.

18
00:01:22,124 --> 00:01:23,458
I've got two great spots in mind.

19
00:01:23,542 --> 00:01:24,543
-Yeah?
-Really, now.

20
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,753
I really wanted a group photo
that includes all seven of us

21
00:01:26,837 --> 00:01:27,921
with Sedona in the background.

22
00:01:28,005 --> 00:01:29,631
-Nice.
-Great. Nice idea.

23
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:30,799
Let's go with that.

24
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:32,968
Let's make our way to
the photo shoot location. Yeah?

25
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:34,344
I'm down. Let's get moving.

26
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:36,597
It's been ages since the seven of us
walked together like this.

27
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,681
That's true.

28
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:40,017
-We didn't walk at all yesterday.
-Nope, we sat around on our butts.

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,268
We had a scrumptious meal though.

30
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:42,811
-Man, did we eat.
-You know it.

31
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,313
-Ain't that the truth.
-That's all right.

32
00:01:44,396 --> 00:01:47,107
-Travis Japan is always moving forward.
-[band members exclaim]

33
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,191
-Cringe.
-Say what?

34
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:50,193
-You callin' him cringe?
-[Machu] Zuya-nii!

35
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:53,155
-The sunlight through the leaves is nice.
-What a nice hidden spot.

36
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:57,451
This is it, the real Sedona.

37
00:01:57,534 --> 00:01:58,535
Let's go, Sedona!

38
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:00,537
Sedona's just like Ikspiari,
the gateway to Tokyo Disneyland.

39
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,748
-[band members, in English] Hi! Hello!
-[tourists] Hi!

40
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:05,542
-Hello! Hello!
-[tourists] Hello, how are you?

41
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,462
[in Japanese] Is this the right way?

42
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:09,629
Wanna switch spots?

43
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:11,298
-'Preciate it.
-No prob.

44
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:13,342
-How's the setup, Shime?
-Want me to take over?

45
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:15,260
No, stay there.
What did we switch spots for?

46
00:02:15,344 --> 00:02:17,262
-Lookin' good.
-Press the timer.

47
00:02:17,346 --> 00:02:19,097
[Shime] Okay. Here we go.

48
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:21,058
-There isn't a countdown. Get ready, guys.
-It's going!

49
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,476
Now, dash.

50
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:25,062
This'll be a photo we cherish.

51
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:29,733
Right, let's give off a heartwarming vibe.

52
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:31,777
-How did it turn out?
-It's great. It turned out super.

53
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:33,195
-We're lookin' good.
-We're killing it.

54
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:34,363
-It's rad.
-Isn't it a good one?

55
00:02:34,446 --> 00:02:35,447
You got the money shot.

56
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,823
-Simply put, we killed it.
-Yep.

57
00:02:36,907 --> 00:02:38,825
-Hey. Kura. Take a look.
-You're right.

58
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:41,411
Wowza! [laughing]

59
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:42,496
Machu's high up!

60
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,665
-We lifted him up so high.
-We got a killer shot.

61
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:46,124
We have three to choose from.

62
00:02:46,208 --> 00:02:48,210
-I love that we shot a few different ones.
-What a great view too.

63
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,753
-How nice.
-We've got another one for the books.

64
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:50,837
We captured the Sedona vibe.

65
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:53,882
-I hope this photo will reach many people.
-Sedona is a picturesque little place.

66
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:54,800
Right on.

67
00:03:00,389 --> 00:03:02,099
[narrator, in Japanese] Sedona, Arizona.

68
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,393
There is a place known
for its spiritual energy.

69
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:09,523
Many visitors recount the otherworldly
feeling they get when they're here.

70
00:03:10,482 --> 00:03:13,777
Take one step onto the red soil here,

71
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:17,698
and you'll be met with pure serenity.

72
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:19,449
[♪ upbeat music playing]

73
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:22,869
-It's all connected?
-It is. It's all connected.

74
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:25,288
Noel and Machu wanted to visit
this spiritual hot spot

75
00:03:25,372 --> 00:03:26,581
before departing Sedona.

76
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:31,211
The duo split up from the rest of
the members to enjoy a morning hike.

77
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:33,588
-It's way too early.
-[laughing] Yep.

78
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:35,298
We're two early risers.

79
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:38,009
-It's 7:00 a.m. sharp.
-Yes. But we've got a clear, blue sky.

80
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:39,636
-We sure do.
-Not a cloud in sight.

81
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,762
Yeah. The sky stretches endlessly.

82
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:42,389
Yep. We're hiking up there.

83
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:43,890
-[Machu] That huge rock?
-Can you believe it?

84
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:46,351
-That rock formation's our destination.
-How close are we getting to it?

85
00:03:46,435 --> 00:03:48,437
[Noel] Who knows? Better get started.

86
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,563
[Machu] We're comin' for you!

87
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,898
Meanwhile, the other five…

88
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:54,276
-We've made it to Slide Rock!
-[all cheer] Here we are!

89
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,028
We're gettin' wet!

90
00:03:58,196 --> 00:04:00,073
Machu and Noel left for their hike early.

91
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:02,117
-And we chose the river.
-They went on a hike?

92
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,743
That's right.

93
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:07,414
-Hey, knock it off! Seriously!
-Yo.

94
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:09,583
It's freezing! Watch out for the camera!

95
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:10,500
Camera?

96
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:12,627
-You got this on camera?
-We're here to have a blast!

97
00:04:12,711 --> 00:04:14,004
[Shizu] I'm done with your antics!

98
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:18,258
-Watch it! It's chilly!
-Let's have some fun.

99
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:20,677
[Machu] This is amazing.

100
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:22,929
Seriously, it's the great outdoors.

101
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:26,308
We're trekking through
the real-life Big Thunder Mountain.

102
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:27,559
[Noel] No joke.

103
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:29,811
-Wait, did you hear?
-[Machu] What?

104
00:04:29,895 --> 00:04:33,315
[Noel] Sedona was the inspiration
for Big Thunder Mountain.

105
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:34,775
-No kidding!
-That's right.

106
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:41,031
Walt Disney based the ride on the town
after visiting himself.

107
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:44,493
[Machu] No kidding. And we're at
the very place Walt Disney came.

108
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:46,620
[Noel] Yes, consider it
a pilgrimage of sorts.

109
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:47,704
Geez, well I feel honored.

110
00:04:47,788 --> 00:04:50,081
We're honored to follow
in Walt Disney's footsteps.

111
00:04:50,165 --> 00:04:52,334
[Machu] You spent the entire week
neck-deep in taco-making?

112
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,835
It was a tacolicious week,
I tell you what.

113
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:55,879
-Those tacos were the bomb. Seriously.
-Then it was worthwhile.

114
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:59,716
You'd think I'm exaggerating,
but those tacos were life-changing.

115
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,551
So when we order catering
for our live shows,

116
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:03,011
can we request tacos from you?

117
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:04,304
-Easily.
-That's the best.

118
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:06,139
[Noel] I prefer to be on the stage though.

119
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:07,474
-[Machu] Do both.
-[both laugh]

120
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,476
Perform on stage and cater the food.

121
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:10,560
I'll do both.

122
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,687
[Machu] This view is phenomenal.

123
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:16,024
I keep repeating myself, but it really is
like a real-life Big Thunder Mountain.

124
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,484
[Noel laughs] Agreed.

125
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:20,737
[exclaims]

126
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:22,447
You got me!

127
00:05:22,531 --> 00:05:24,616
-He's done it now.
-Stop it! No, no!

128
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:28,328
Seriously, I'll end up hurt!

129
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:30,247
-Don't mess with me. Hands off!
-Get 'em, get 'em.

130
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:34,793
-Shoot, shoot! I'm not joking anymore!
-Play nice.

131
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:35,961
[screams]

132
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:37,587
Time to scram.

133
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:39,172
I hurt my knee!

134
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:43,051
[Genta] I'm callin' truce!
Stop it, you jerks!

135
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:47,055
You better not do this! Hey!
You Team A's full of…

136
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:48,598
-Hey!
-I'm not going down!

137
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:51,184
Never!

138
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:54,771
[laughing]

139
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:59,025
It's freezing! I'ma get hypothermia!

140
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:03,572
Wait, wait! Stop!

141
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:06,241
[screams, shrieks]

142
00:06:07,826 --> 00:06:10,537
It's freezing! It's punishingly cold!

143
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,539
[Noel] Did you interact with many locals?

144
00:06:13,123 --> 00:06:14,124
[Machu] I sure did.

145
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:18,461
I made a hat with a nice hatmaker
and stuff.

146
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:19,546
[Noel] Okay, okay.

147
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,341
[Machu] We also spoke
to a bunch of shopkeepers.

148
00:06:23,425 --> 00:06:24,426
[Noel] Of course you did.

149
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:30,307
It's not every day
you're immersed in live English.

150
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,641
[Machu] It's true.

151
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:36,146
[Noel] And this region, so New Mexico,

152
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:41,443
Arizona, and the Southwest at large,
has a large Hispanic population.

153
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:47,115
We're both trying to communicate
using imperfect English.

154
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:48,199
[Machu] I know what you mean.

155
00:06:48,283 --> 00:06:49,743
I love the heartfelt communication
we get out of it.

156
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:52,037
Yes. We understand each other.

157
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,121
Exactly.

158
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:55,123
What a fantastic view.

159
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:56,333
I love it.

160
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:58,001
-Good work making it this far.
-Likewise.

161
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:00,170
-We've got a long way to go. [chuckles]
-[laughs]

162
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,130
-We won't be done anytime soon.
-No kidding.

163
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:04,049
-Hold on.
-My goodness, this view is to die for.

164
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,550
What a magnificent view.

165
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:07,093
Only in Sedona.

166
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:09,512
Only in Sedona indeed.

167
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:12,390
These reds and greens
are so iconic to Sedona.

168
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:13,433
Hup.

169
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:15,352
Incredible.

170
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,523
[sighs] What a nice breeze.

171
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:25,945
It doesn't feel real.

172
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:28,031
No, it doesn't.

173
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:29,574
-Shall we keep going?
-We shall.

174
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:31,826
Where's the goal?

175
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:33,828
[tourist] Wow!

176
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:36,373
They said, "Wow." I feel them.

177
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:37,457
Same.

178
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:40,043
Hup.

179
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:42,045
Wow.

180
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:44,005
-It already looks breathtaking.
-Isn't this something?

181
00:07:44,089 --> 00:07:45,090
Just wow.

182
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:47,592
-[Umi] Oh, Shime.
-[Shizu] Shime.

183
00:07:47,676 --> 00:07:50,387
Didn't think we'd spare only you,
now, did you?

184
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,722
-Leave it, we've got a change of clothes.
-I'll take you on.

185
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:56,351
Crap, he means business.

186
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:03,775
We were surrounded by nature
this entire trip.

187
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:06,611
I've become quite comfortable around it.

188
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:11,616
Not too long ago,
I would've hated jumping in the water.

189
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,118
What was your trip like?

190
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:15,704
We visited all sorts of towns…

191
00:08:15,787 --> 00:08:18,206
-Right, right.
-…and learned their history.

192
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:20,792
They told us about the history
behind turquoise jewelry,

193
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:23,336
-how they're made and such.
-I see.

194
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:27,799
We also learned the role turquoise plays
in the Native American culture,

195
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:30,301
-and the significance of wearing it.
-I see, I see.

196
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:33,888
We got a deep look into their culture.

197
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:35,140
-How wonderful.
-It really was.

198
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:38,393
-So, we were chatting yesterday.
-Right, right.

199
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:42,272
And we all agreed you were
into this trip the most.

200
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:45,358
-[laughing] Really?
-None of us expected that.

201
00:08:45,442 --> 00:08:46,526
-You talked about me?
-We did.

202
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:48,111
You're a homebody

203
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:50,613
-who loves to play video games.
-Right.

204
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:51,781
It's what I like to do.

205
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:55,118
So we didn't know
if you were enjoying this trip.

206
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,536
Right, right, right.

207
00:08:56,619 --> 00:09:00,290
But yesterday at the dinner,
we all felt you got the most out of it.

208
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:03,084
I had a blast. It was such a great trip.

209
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:06,880
I visited many sites.
Really, every bit of it was fun.

210
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:08,298
I'm even having fun hanging out here.

211
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,883
It's been a while since
I last took a dip in a river…

212
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,134
Right, right.

213
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,844
…and I'm thinking, "This is unbeatable."

214
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:14,971
[Shime exclaims]

215
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:18,475
[screams]

216
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:21,227
-Got 'em! [laughing]
-It's freezing!

217
00:09:27,317 --> 00:09:29,277
Haven't heard you that loud in a while.

218
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,029
Wait, are we supposed to climb up here?

219
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:33,156
-No way.
-It's ridiculously steep.

220
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:35,492
-What a rough trail. Hold on, hold on.
-I need a minute.

221
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:37,744
-[Noel] It's such a steep trail.
-[Machu] I can't believe it.

222
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:39,370
It's too soon to check out
the view behind us.

223
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:42,207
-You're right. Good insight.
-I'll wait on it.

224
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,876
-"Too soon to look back."
-[Machu chuckles]

225
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:47,003
-That's my quote of the day.
-[Noel] There it is.

226
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:49,255
[grunts]

227
00:09:49,339 --> 00:09:52,175
-[Noel] Incredible! I can't believe this.
-It's unbelievable.

228
00:09:52,258 --> 00:09:53,259
It really is.

229
00:09:53,343 --> 00:09:55,637
-It's more of a cliff than a trail.
-[Machu] We're scaling a wall.

230
00:10:00,058 --> 00:10:01,559
[both grunting]

231
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:03,144
Hup.

232
00:10:05,063 --> 00:10:07,190
-[Noel] Seriously, this…
-[Machu] Hup-ho.

233
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,651
Scaling the Cathedral Rock in one go,

234
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:12,654
no stops in between,
it's just as exciting as being on stage.

235
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,239
I honestly feel that.

236
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:19,244
-Do you know which part of the cactus…
-Yeah?

237
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:21,204
…is the leaves?

238
00:10:22,831 --> 00:10:24,582
-Not these parts?
-[chuckles]

239
00:10:24,666 --> 00:10:28,169
That's what you'd think, right?
It's actually the needles.

240
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,879
[Machu] What? I would've never guessed.

241
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:31,714
[Noel] Isn't it intriguing?

242
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:34,425
To start, I had no idea
a cactus was shaped like this.

243
00:10:34,509 --> 00:10:35,510
[Noel laughs]

244
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,470
[Machu] I thought,
"Aren't they supposed to be round?"

245
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:39,806
[Noel] Most people imagine succulents
when they hear cactus.

246
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:40,723
Is that why?

247
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:41,891
My goodness!

248
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:42,976
[Noel] Hold on.

249
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:44,769
TJ!

250
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,729
[Machu laughing] It's echoey.

251
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:49,983
Travis Japan!

252
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:53,987
Travis Japan!

253
00:10:54,863 --> 00:10:56,156
[laughing]

254
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:58,992
[Machu shrieks, laughs]

255
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:01,661
[Noel] I hear a dog.
Guess there's a feral dog somewhere.

256
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:05,915
Look, it says "End of Trail."

257
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:07,834
-We made it!
-At last!

258
00:11:09,878 --> 00:11:12,589
-We actually did it!
-[cheers]

259
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:13,965
This is surreal.

260
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:20,054
You'd never understand this feeling
unless you hike up here yourself.

261
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:21,973
-Yeah.
-This overwhelming feeling.

262
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:26,519
[Noel] It's like Chaka said yesterday.
We can share a photo of this place…

263
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:27,770
Yes.

264
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:29,981
…but you have to see this in person
to understand.

265
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,441
-It's indescribable.
-Exactly.

266
00:11:32,901 --> 00:11:36,362
This is amazing. It's all real.

267
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:37,989
It's deeply moving.

268
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,036
I know I said I won't look behind me
til I reach the top, but…

269
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,120
Right.

270
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:47,665
-The best view was in front of me.
-[chuckles]

271
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:49,918
What an incredible view.

272
00:11:51,878 --> 00:11:53,421
You said this place is
a spiritual hot spot, right?

273
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:54,505
Right.

274
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:58,676
-Shall we feel the spiritual energy here?
-Let's do it.

275
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:03,097
[Noel exclaims]

276
00:12:04,349 --> 00:12:05,391
[Noel] This is incredible!

277
00:12:05,934 --> 00:12:07,185
Talk about a precipice.

278
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:11,314
-[chuckles]
-Wow.

279
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:15,109
I'm getting chills.

280
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,529
[♪ serene pipe music playing]

281
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:35,755
-[♪ music continues]
-[no audible dialogue]

282
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,707
-Whoo!
-Let's go!

283
00:14:34,791 --> 00:14:36,918
-Let's go!
-Comin'!

284
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,836
-Time to hit the road.
-Let's go.

285
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,338
-Let's go, let's go.
-Let's get going.

286
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:41,756
Time to get outta here.

287
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:43,049
-We've got our own car.
-Hop in, guys.

288
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:45,426
-What a big car.
-[in English] Thank you.

289
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:50,890
[in Japanese] All right.

290
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:52,141
Time to hit the road.

291
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:53,392
Let's get goin'!

292
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,020
Hup.

293
00:14:56,104 --> 00:14:57,105
I'll take this seat.

294
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:01,734
[Noel] Been a while since
we've last been in a car together.

295
00:15:01,818 --> 00:15:02,819
So it has.

296
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,445
Heck yes. Noel's takin' the wheel.

297
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:05,530
-Yeah!
-It's been a while.

298
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:07,990
-A bit cramped in here.
-I'll scoot up.

299
00:15:08,074 --> 00:15:09,075
Here we go.

300
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:12,120
-Let's go, let's go! Time for a road trip!
-We're counting on you, Noel!

301
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,331
[all cheering]

302
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:20,253
[♪ blues music playing]

303
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:24,382
[Machu] So it begins.

304
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,259
[Genta] Finally, all seven of us
in a car together.

305
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:28,261
-Right?
-It's been a while.

306
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,054
-Me, I'm content…
-Right?

307
00:15:30,138 --> 00:15:32,849
…just spending time with you guys.

308
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:35,268
But you aren't in your usual seats.

309
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:36,894
-Nice observation.
-True that.

310
00:15:36,978 --> 00:15:39,355
-[Noel] My nerves are kicking in.
-[laughs]

311
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:42,525
[Noel] I looked forward to this
for the past week.

312
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:44,986
The seven of us have finally hit the road.

313
00:15:45,987 --> 00:15:51,409
Our next destination is a city close
to Travis Japan's heart, Los Angeles.

314
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,412
[in English] Sixty-six.

315
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,038
[in Japanese] Route 66.

316
00:15:56,873 --> 00:15:59,292
I wonder if Route 66
has historical significance?

317
00:15:59,375 --> 00:16:04,380
During the Gold Rush, laborers traveled
on this route to reach the west coast,

318
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:08,718
hoping to strike gold or find jobs.

319
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,303
From east to west.

320
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:13,973
[Noel] Right. It was a road of dreams.

321
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,266
Interesting.

322
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:17,768
Which means, originally,
it wasn't maintained this well.

323
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:20,104
[Noel] That's right.
It must've gotten paved over time.

324
00:16:20,188 --> 00:16:21,230
[Shime] I see.

325
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:25,610
And now, we, the aspiring musicians,
are traveling this very road of dreams.

326
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,195
-It gives me chills.
-That's deep!

327
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:29,071
-You're a poet today.
-That hit me right in the feels.

328
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:47,215
[narrator] Seligman, Arizona.

329
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:53,763
This legendary town breathed new life
into the Mother Road.

330
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:56,766
On this main street
where time stands still,

331
00:16:56,849 --> 00:17:00,228
traces of the American dream linger.

332
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,440
-[laughs]
-That's a cute photo spot.

333
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:06,525
What do you think about that stand-in?
Let's poke our heads out of it.

334
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:07,610
What? I wanna do it.

335
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:11,739
What? Let's go, let's go!
Let's snap a photo. Let's do it!

336
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:15,868
Right there.

337
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,328
-I love it! Cute.
-You guys look cute.

338
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,121
You look great.

339
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:20,539
[Umi] You guys are synced up!

340
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:22,541
Best buddies.

341
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:25,753
-You're lookin' great!
-Thanks.

342
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:26,837
-Here, here.
-Thank you.

343
00:17:26,921 --> 00:17:28,214
Next, next.

344
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:29,632
-Do you want a photo, Umi?
-Move along, guys.

345
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:30,800
-Hey, someone…
-Hurry, get in the spot.

346
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:31,884
Shizuya's…

347
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:33,636
Wait, he needs a buddy!
Shizuya's by himself.

348
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,054
-He needs a buddy.
-What about Chaka?

349
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,222
[Umi] He went somewhere.

350
00:17:36,305 --> 00:17:38,182
[Shime] Say cheese.

351
00:17:38,266 --> 00:17:39,517
Snappity-snap.

352
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:41,852
-Lookin' cute.
-You look great.

353
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:42,979
-Nice!
-Thanks.

354
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,063
Thanks, guys!

355
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,148
[♪ country blues music playing]

356
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:27,231
[narrator] This town's glory days
ended with the gold mine.

357
00:18:27,315 --> 00:18:30,610
Now, it's a popular tourist spot
where wild burros roam.

358
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:35,281
It's a lively town where one can
step into the world of Old Westerns.

359
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:38,159
-I saw burros. Did you?
-There are a ton of burros here.

360
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:42,747
Well… They're wild.
Best to steer clear of them.

361
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:45,499
-Back in the day…
-Do you think they'd kick?

362
00:18:45,583 --> 00:18:48,085
…laborers used burros to transport oil.

363
00:18:48,169 --> 00:18:49,545
-[Noel] That's why they're still around.
-[Shizu] Yep.

364
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,422
-And now, they roam freely?
-That's a perfect two shot.

365
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:52,923
I believe so.

366
00:18:53,007 --> 00:18:54,133
-Cute.
-How cute.

367
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,635
-What a friendly burro.
-It's docile.

368
00:18:55,718 --> 00:18:56,719
See ya, buddy.

369
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:59,305
[burro brays]

370
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:05,603
[narrator] The ancestors of these friendly
burros once worked alongside miners.

371
00:19:06,354 --> 00:19:09,148
In the present day, these friendly
creatures are the stars of this town.

372
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,692
[Shime] Wait, wait, wait, wait…

373
00:19:11,776 --> 00:19:14,445
-You'll get some, all right?
-[Noel] How cute! This little…

374
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,529
Can I pet you?

375
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:17,448
-[Umi] You made a new friend.
-[Shime] Right?

376
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:21,327
To reward horses, you pat them right here
and say, "Good job."

377
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:22,411
Really?

378
00:19:23,037 --> 00:19:24,246
Good job.

379
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:26,207
-I did it all the time in my school club.
-Good job.

380
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,291
Right?

381
00:19:27,375 --> 00:19:29,752
-Were you in the equestrian club?
-I was in the equestrian club.

382
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:30,836
Right?

383
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,963
It must be where Noel learned
to "horse around."

384
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:34,674
-The horses taught him.
-No, no.

385
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:35,800
-They fought.
-I'm all out.

386
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:36,884
Let's get going. Let's move on.

387
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:37,968
-Here.
-Okay?

388
00:19:38,052 --> 00:19:41,180
I told you, I don't have anymore.

389
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:43,140
See? No more.

390
00:19:43,224 --> 00:19:44,308
[Umi] Thanks for playing with us.

391
00:19:44,392 --> 00:19:48,104
-Okay, last little bit.
-That's the very last one. Just for you.

392
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,397
Please. No more. Now, go away.

393
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,482
-They gave him a shake down.
-I mean it. I'm all emptied out.

394
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:53,484
[Shime] I'll leave this here, all right?
Sorry.

395
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:54,402
I was startled.

396
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:56,195
-I thought it was Genta. Nope.
-Hey, everyone!

397
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:57,571
I tossed some out
so they'd stop chasing me.

398
00:19:57,655 --> 00:19:59,115
They came at me since
I was close to Machu.

399
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,741
This was a great little stop. Bye-bye!

400
00:20:00,825 --> 00:20:02,159
-Right this way, please.
-'Til next time!

401
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:04,203
-Are we grabbing food?
-Yeah.

402
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,287
Sorry, not here.

403
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:08,457
Is this a restaurant?
That's what it says here.

404
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:10,751
There are too many establishments.

405
00:20:11,502 --> 00:20:12,962
Here we go. This is it. Finally!

406
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:14,922
[narrator] This is the Oatman Hotel.

407
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:19,260
It's a historic hotel where many
Old Western stars and celebrities stayed.

408
00:20:20,094 --> 00:20:23,597
The nights the stars spent here
still live on in this hotel.

409
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:29,270
Each dollar bill plastered on the walls
tells a tale of the travelers' dreams.

410
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:32,690
Here, time and money alike
turn into memories.

411
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:35,276
-Let's go, let's go, let's go.
-[Noel] What? How fascinating.

412
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:36,694
What the heck?

413
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:38,070
Holy smokes.

414
00:20:38,154 --> 00:20:39,905
[♪ gospel song playing]

415
00:20:39,989 --> 00:20:41,449
Are these all bills?

416
00:20:42,867 --> 00:20:43,868
Just what is this about?

417
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:47,538
The bills are plastered
up and down the wall.

418
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:48,622
It's incredible.

419
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:51,584
Thousands of dollars cover the walls!

420
00:20:51,667 --> 00:20:54,920
-These are all dollar bills.
-I'll have Wild West Buffalo Wings.

421
00:20:55,004 --> 00:20:56,464
-[in English] Wings?
-Yes.

422
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:04,889
-Excuse me?
-Yes.

423
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:09,351
So, why so many dollars in here?

424
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,228
-How many? Why are there so many dollars?
-Yeah.

425
00:21:11,312 --> 00:21:13,814
So, when the miners were here
mining for gold,

426
00:21:13,898 --> 00:21:15,149
they would get paid

427
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:17,234
and they didn't wanna take the money
out to the mines,

428
00:21:17,318 --> 00:21:19,487
'cause they would lose it
or not make it back.

429
00:21:19,570 --> 00:21:21,655
So, they'd write their name on it,
stick it to the walls

430
00:21:21,739 --> 00:21:25,451
so they could pay for a haircut,
bar tab, hotel room,

431
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:29,663
and that's how it originally started
back in the '30s and '40s.

432
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:32,666
Um, and there's close to
half a million dollars here.

433
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,710
-Half a million?
-Half a million? Wow.

434
00:21:34,794 --> 00:21:36,962
-[Noel] Really? Half a million?
-Yep. Yep.

435
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:38,964
It's on top, and top,
and top of each other.

436
00:21:39,048 --> 00:21:40,132
Is it kind of…

437
00:21:40,216 --> 00:21:44,011
-Uh, so many bills for… Is kind of…
-[server] Yes.

438
00:21:44,887 --> 00:21:47,097
For, like, to pay for a haircut.

439
00:21:47,181 --> 00:21:50,017
-A haircut?
-Everything back then was five cents.

440
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:52,436
-So, one dollar, you had all the change.
-Really?

441
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:55,606
-So, it's kind of like a bank.
-A bank…

442
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:57,274
-Okay. Okay.
-Yeah. Okay.

443
00:21:57,358 --> 00:21:58,359
Okay.

444
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:03,948
So, do we need to steal the…
our bills for here with our--

445
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:05,866
The last person that stole,

446
00:22:05,950 --> 00:22:07,785
they got shot
and they're buried in the back,

447
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:08,869
so you better be careful.

448
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:10,120
[Noel] Okay. Got it.

449
00:22:10,204 --> 00:22:12,373
-Thank you. Sorry. Thank you.
-Yeah.

450
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:15,751
[in Japanese] All right, mining means
"to dig for precious ores."

451
00:22:15,835 --> 00:22:19,213
These bills belonged to the miners
who flocked here during the Gold Rush

452
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:21,382
-hoping to strike gold.
-[Shizu] That tracks.

453
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:22,842
-That's why, the money…
-Yes.

454
00:22:22,925 --> 00:22:25,761
-First time eating it deep-fried.
-That's right.

455
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:28,055
-This is delicious.
-It hits the spot.

456
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:29,557
[Shizu] We've got a following of flies.

457
00:22:30,558 --> 00:22:32,434
[Genta] It's good to have a following,
even if they're flies.

458
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:33,602
[Shizu] It's important.

459
00:22:33,686 --> 00:22:35,813
-[in English] We have already three, so…
-Thank you.

460
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:36,897
Thank you.

461
00:22:36,981 --> 00:22:38,232
[Shime] Miner Burger.

462
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:39,567
-[in Japanese] Here, use this.
-Thank you.

463
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:41,235
[Noel] Miner means "someone who mines."

464
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:42,945
Maybe there's history behind
this burger too.

465
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:44,029
[Shime] I see.

466
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:47,658
-[in English] Hot wings.
-Wow.

467
00:22:47,741 --> 00:22:49,243
-Hot Buffalo Wings.
-Hot wings here.

468
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:51,287
-Okay. Crispy chicken salad.
-Doesn't it look tasty?

469
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:52,204
-Crispy, please.
-Yep.

470
00:22:52,288 --> 00:22:53,581
-There you go.
-Doesn't it?

471
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:58,335
Buffalo burger, onion rings,
American cheese.

472
00:22:58,419 --> 00:22:59,837
-American cheese.
-American cheese.

473
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,005
Here you go.

474
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:02,590
-[in Japanese] That's good.
-Time to dig in.

475
00:23:02,673 --> 00:23:04,008
-Diggin' in!
-Digging in!

476
00:23:05,926 --> 00:23:06,969
Awesome.

477
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:08,846
This is the best.

478
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:09,972
Yum.

479
00:23:11,682 --> 00:23:13,142
It's supreme.

480
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:14,268
Delicious.

481
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:16,020
-It's very good.
-Yum.

482
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:18,564
-My tummy is rejoicing.
-So good.

483
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:19,648
This is bliss.

484
00:23:22,318 --> 00:23:23,569
[Shizu] The veggies are good too.

485
00:23:24,069 --> 00:23:26,655
-It's friggin' good.
-Thanks for finding a great spot.

486
00:23:26,739 --> 00:23:27,907
-No prob.
-This is so good.

487
00:23:27,990 --> 00:23:29,325
-Thanks.
-Right? Isn't it delicious?

488
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:31,243
-I happened to come across it.
-[Genta exclaiming] Mmm!

489
00:23:36,707 --> 00:23:37,708
So yummy.

490
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:40,210
Let's order this food
for rehearsal breaks.

491
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:42,671
-Nice.
-Wanna order some?

492
00:23:42,755 --> 00:23:43,756
We can't.

493
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:47,051
The buns are the best part.
They're crispy.

494
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:49,345
-Indeed, they are crispy and delicious.
-You copied me.

495
00:23:49,428 --> 00:23:52,389
Yeah, these buns hit the spot!
Love their crispy texture.

496
00:23:52,473 --> 00:23:53,891
That's the fourth time.

497
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:54,975
It's getting a bit spicy.

498
00:23:55,059 --> 00:23:56,393
[Noel] Is the buffalo burger gamy?

499
00:23:57,519 --> 00:24:00,064
[Umi] Buffalo? Not at all.
It's the same as a classic burger.

500
00:24:00,147 --> 00:24:02,107
-Actually?
-There's nothing to it, really.

501
00:24:02,191 --> 00:24:03,567
It's no different from a classic burger.

502
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:05,027
It's about as basic a burger
as you can get.

503
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:06,779
American units confuse me.

504
00:24:08,489 --> 00:24:10,908
-They confuse me too.
-No kidding.

505
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:13,410
There are ounces and gallons,
and one gallon equals 3.8 liters.

506
00:24:13,494 --> 00:24:15,329
Oh, and 12 ounces make up a gallon.

507
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:17,289
Okay, I'm completely lost.

508
00:24:17,373 --> 00:24:19,124
-[Machu] Fahrenheit is a mystery to me.
-I'm on the same boat.

509
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:21,001
-It is a different ball game.
-For temperature…

510
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:24,672
For temperature, take Celsius,
multiply it by 9/5th,

511
00:24:24,755 --> 00:24:27,925
then add 32 to convert it to Fahrenheit.

512
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:29,134
A toddler could solve that.

513
00:24:29,218 --> 00:24:30,844
-You caught all that?
-So…

514
00:24:31,553 --> 00:24:34,807
Let's say the temp on the AC is set to 70.

515
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,517
What is that in Celsius?

516
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:39,937
Subtract 32 from 70, then you get 38.

517
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:46,193
You take 5/9th of 38, which equals…
Seven, five… It's about…

518
00:24:48,946 --> 00:24:50,030
-Well?
-Twenty…

519
00:24:50,114 --> 00:24:53,117
-About twenty-two, three degrees Celsius?
-Twenty… I see. Maybe? That tracks.

520
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,369
-Sounds about right.
-We just need to know the approximate.

521
00:24:55,452 --> 00:24:58,914
-The approximate's all we wanna know.
-Noel's equation is all we need.

522
00:24:58,998 --> 00:25:00,249
So 70 is about 22.

523
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,793
I usually set the AC to 73.

524
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:03,919
-Me too.
-Same.

525
00:25:04,003 --> 00:25:05,546
-Seventy's a bit chilly.
-A bit, yeah.

526
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:07,131
-Seventy's chilly.
-And 60 is sweater weather.

527
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:08,382
-Sixty's pretty chilly.
-Yeah.

528
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:11,510
Seventy-three's the best temperature
to wake up to.

529
00:25:13,012 --> 00:25:15,389
[Noel]
Is Machu gonna drive the second leg?

530
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:17,349
-Wait, I am?
-I'm only saying. If you can't…

531
00:25:17,433 --> 00:25:19,018
-[Machu] We need a plan.
-[Noel] What should we do?

532
00:25:19,101 --> 00:25:20,853
-Yeah, really though.
-I don't mind.

533
00:25:25,774 --> 00:25:28,402
-Shall we hit the road?
-We already are!

534
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:32,031
Oh, we're already on the way!

535
00:25:32,114 --> 00:25:33,824
Thanks, Machu!

536
00:25:33,907 --> 00:25:35,868
Let's go!

537
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:40,122
I don't drive on these roads often.

538
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:41,999
-Alongside the burros.
-Burros, everywhere.

539
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:44,543
I'd get freaked out if one of them
jumped in front of the car.

540
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:46,962
-[Umi] Be confident.
-Burros don't cross the street in Japan.

541
00:25:48,630 --> 00:25:49,631
[Machu] Hello, friend.

542
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:51,383
[Shime] Animals don't jump
in front of cars in Japan, do they?

543
00:25:51,467 --> 00:25:53,177
-[Shizu] Don't think so.
-Hello, there.

544
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:54,261
Wait, hold on!

545
00:25:54,344 --> 00:25:55,679
-Get outta the way!
-Go right!

546
00:25:55,763 --> 00:25:57,306
-Wanna turn to the right?
-Let's do it.

547
00:25:57,389 --> 00:25:58,682
-Let's go.
-Watch the one to the right.

548
00:25:58,766 --> 00:26:00,768
-What about behind the car?
-We're good.

549
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:02,603
Watch out! That was close.

550
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:07,107
-Make up your mind, burro!
-Another one incoming to the right.

551
00:26:07,191 --> 00:26:08,442
Oh, what?

552
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:10,611
Hey now!

553
00:26:10,694 --> 00:26:12,488
-Oh, come on.
-We don't have treats for you!

554
00:26:12,571 --> 00:26:14,323
We don't have any more!

555
00:26:14,406 --> 00:26:15,574
What's this, a safari park?

556
00:26:15,657 --> 00:26:17,159
-We're outta stock!
-This is too funny.

557
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:18,368
They got us.

558
00:26:18,452 --> 00:26:19,661
-Just give up.
-Leave it to me.

559
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:22,581
-I'll get them outta our way.
-Wait!

560
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:27,336
-This might work.
-He looks like he's got treats for them.

561
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:28,670
-Wait, how…
-Whoa, whoa!

562
00:26:28,754 --> 00:26:30,089
It ran off!

563
00:26:31,965 --> 00:26:32,966
What?

564
00:26:34,218 --> 00:26:35,636
Here they come…

565
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:37,513
Watch out. Coming up behind you, Genta.

566
00:26:38,222 --> 00:26:41,100
Genta, wait… wait, wait, wait.
Genta, behind you!

567
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:42,810
Just pull over.

568
00:26:42,893 --> 00:26:45,229
Hold on, he left the door open.

569
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:46,647
-Let's take a picture.
-Wait. Oh no, Genta!

570
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:48,357
-This burro's trying to come in!
-The door's wide open!

571
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:51,026
-Oh no! It wants to come inside! Crap!
-Close the door, hurry!

572
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:52,361
-Go ahead, full speed.
-Slam it shut!

573
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,071
-Now, go! Pedal to the metal!
-Thanks.

574
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:55,280
-Go left.
-You'll be missed, Genta.

575
00:26:55,364 --> 00:26:57,157
It's fine, they're not in the way.
You won't crash into them.

576
00:26:57,241 --> 00:27:00,327
-Shall we say our farewell to Genta?
-Let's say bye to Genta.

577
00:27:02,037 --> 00:27:04,081
-Oh no…
-Anything behind us?

578
00:27:04,164 --> 00:27:05,624
-You're good.
-You're in the lane.

579
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,251
Let's go. We're good, we're good.

580
00:27:10,754 --> 00:27:11,964
[chuckling]

581
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:13,757
-Nice going!
-Thank you.

582
00:27:13,841 --> 00:27:16,426
-Great job, Genta.
-How was my dance?

583
00:27:16,510 --> 00:27:18,929
You busted out your dance moves.
Don't forget to buckle up.

584
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,348
Now the burros are galloping!

585
00:27:22,349 --> 00:27:24,393
-What's up with them?
-Machu, we're surrounded!

586
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:25,936
Machu, can we take the left lane instead?

587
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:27,229
-We're good.
-Are there cars coming?

588
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,398
I know what it is.
It's time for burros to go home.

589
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:30,482
-Is it their curfew?
-Nice.

590
00:27:30,566 --> 00:27:32,150
-These burros have a curfew.
-They have a curfew.

591
00:27:32,234 --> 00:27:34,570
-That's why they're in a hurry.
-That explains it.

592
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:36,822
-This isn't normal.
-Things are gettin' desperate.

593
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:39,199
-Right?
-I never expected this to happen.

594
00:27:39,283 --> 00:27:40,576
[Shizu] What a tough drive.

595
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:59,386
The sun's blindin'. It's in my eyes.

596
00:27:59,469 --> 00:28:01,930
-It was such a nice trip.
-I know, right?

597
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:03,348
-What a nice trip.
-It was the best.

598
00:28:03,432 --> 00:28:05,767
-It sure was.
-Yeah. It was over before I knew it.

599
00:28:06,435 --> 00:28:07,978
It came and went all too fast.

600
00:28:08,061 --> 00:28:09,688
-In the blink of an eye.
-It went by in a flash.

601
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:11,899
The trip went by fast,
but at the same time,

602
00:28:11,982 --> 00:28:14,610
I felt as if I haven't
seen you guys in ages.

603
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:15,736
-Right, right.
-Yeah.

604
00:28:15,819 --> 00:28:17,946
-It's a strange sensation.
-I know what you mean.

605
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:22,910
This trip came to a close.
We were divided up into three teams.

606
00:28:22,993 --> 00:28:27,998
Because of it, I came to know

607
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:31,585
each member's personality,
or rather, their values.

608
00:28:31,668 --> 00:28:37,841
I'm glad I got to go on a summer trip
with Noel's itinerary in the US.

609
00:28:37,925 --> 00:28:39,343
-It was the best.
-It was so fun.

610
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:43,138
Remember when we all cried
our eyes out during the reunion?

611
00:28:44,222 --> 00:28:50,145
Those tears came from
the deepest part of my heart.

612
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:52,022
-It was a good cry.
-Right.

613
00:28:52,105 --> 00:28:54,399
I kept remembering moments from AGT.

614
00:28:54,483 --> 00:28:55,484
I see.

615
00:28:55,567 --> 00:29:00,072
It was similar to how emotions ran high
at the end of the first audition.

616
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:01,156
Right, right.

617
00:29:01,239 --> 00:29:03,283
-It takes me back.
-I feel you.

618
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:04,409
It was unforgettable.

619
00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:06,787
You only cry like that
a few times in your life.

620
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,539
-Exactly. It's a rare occasion.
-I haven't felt this way in a while.

621
00:29:09,623 --> 00:29:13,919
We were brought to tears
because of our bond.

622
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:15,879
-Right.
-Looking back,

623
00:29:15,963 --> 00:29:21,134
it felt as though we were still connected,
although we were miles apart.

624
00:29:21,218 --> 00:29:24,137
-It's true.
-Maybe it was the tequila.

625
00:29:24,221 --> 00:29:26,932
-But man, did we bawl like babies.
-Could've been the alcohol.

626
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:28,850
-Chaka, you were downing shots.
-I sure was.

627
00:29:29,351 --> 00:29:32,396
There's one thing I can say for certain.
I'm grateful for all of you.

628
00:29:32,479 --> 00:29:35,190
Sometimes, I get wrapped up in my head.

629
00:29:35,273 --> 00:29:39,611
It's you who always pull me out
in those moments.

630
00:29:39,695 --> 00:29:42,948
We support each other
with our differences.

631
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:45,784
That's rad.

632
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:48,078
-Says Chaka as he drives.
-Was that cool, or what?

633
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:49,997
You know, I can see the sun
reflecting off your sunglasses.

634
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:52,541
-It's making your face sparkle.
-How are you even able to see?

635
00:29:53,250 --> 00:29:54,251
The sun is blinding.

636
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:56,294
-Wait, I'm getting a bit scared.
-Oh no, oh no.

637
00:29:56,378 --> 00:29:57,713
Just lower the vanity mirror.

638
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:59,214
-That's ingenious. Nice!
-It's way too bright.

639
00:29:59,297 --> 00:30:01,591
You said something profound.
What was it again?

640
00:30:02,175 --> 00:30:04,177
-Don't forget it.
-Care to repeat it?

641
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:07,597
-[Noel] We keep going straight.
-On and on and on.

642
00:30:07,681 --> 00:30:10,308
-[Noel] The road never ends.
-The road stretches on.

643
00:30:10,392 --> 00:30:13,478
-What a beautiful view.
-[all exclaim]

644
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:17,357
-[whooping]
-Shall we travel around?

645
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:18,734
Guess we shall?

646
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:23,071
-Where should we go next?
-Yeah, what should our next trip be?

647
00:30:23,155 --> 00:30:25,157
[♪ theme song piano version playing]

648
00:30:40,881 --> 00:30:42,883
[♪ song stops]

649
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:46,470
[narrator, in English]
Los Angeles, California.

650
00:30:55,812 --> 00:30:57,022
[in Japanese] Here we are.

651
00:30:57,105 --> 00:30:58,523
Whoa!

652
00:30:58,607 --> 00:31:01,026
Whoa, this brings me back!

653
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:06,782
-Isn't this it?
-Yes, this is the place. We're back!

654
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:08,450
-The height of this ceiling.
-It takes me back.

655
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:10,744
-This must be it.
-Yes. I remember this high ceiling.

656
00:31:11,453 --> 00:31:13,080
[narrator] This is the very studio

657
00:31:13,163 --> 00:31:17,209
where Travis Japan shot the cover
for their debut song, "JUST DANCE!"

658
00:31:18,794 --> 00:31:20,420
Oh, wow.
Remember the changing ceiling lights?

659
00:31:20,504 --> 00:31:21,797
We wore our TJ colors.

660
00:31:23,381 --> 00:31:25,300
-This takes me back.
-Right?

661
00:31:26,927 --> 00:31:29,596
-Shall we do "JUST DANCE!" once?
-Nice idea. I'm down!

662
00:31:29,679 --> 00:31:31,890
-Let's do the chorus only.
-Dance the chorus only?

663
00:31:31,973 --> 00:31:35,644
-We haven't been training, and I'm sore.
-The entire trip was an exercise.

664
00:31:35,727 --> 00:31:37,604
We're only doing the chorus?

665
00:31:37,687 --> 00:31:40,857
-Okay, I'm up for it.
-Where's my position?

666
00:31:40,941 --> 00:31:42,609
Which way's the front of stage?
This direction?

667
00:31:43,318 --> 00:31:44,402
Oh, over here.

668
00:31:44,486 --> 00:31:46,404
-Shall we give it a go?
-Let's do it.

669
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:48,907
What if we start from…

670
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:51,576
Ready?

671
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:53,620
[band members singing]

672
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:15,934
Whoa.

673
00:32:16,017 --> 00:32:17,644
That's "JUST DANCE!" for you!

674
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:19,271
-We did it!
-We killed it!

675
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:21,189
I'm feelin' it.

676
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:22,649
-That was great!
-I'm getting the feels.

677
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:23,733
Shall we snap a photo?

678
00:32:23,817 --> 00:32:26,486
-Oh, let's do it.
-We came all this way, we might as well.

679
00:32:26,570 --> 00:32:29,447
Where should we position the camera?
How about here, to start?

680
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:31,449
Nice.

681
00:32:31,533 --> 00:32:33,535
-Do you remember how we lined up?
-How can I forget?

682
00:32:33,618 --> 00:32:35,579
-Our usual position.
-Here for me?

683
00:32:35,662 --> 00:32:38,248
You want to recreate the debut cover,
including the camera position. Right?

684
00:32:38,331 --> 00:32:40,458
-It's coming back to me.
-Right here.

685
00:32:40,542 --> 00:32:41,751
This feels right.

686
00:32:41,835 --> 00:32:44,754
-I remember clearly. We're doing it right.
-This is our usual position.

687
00:32:44,838 --> 00:32:45,881
That's right.

688
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:48,341
-This brings me back.
-Whoa!

689
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:51,761
-Oh, hold on. This is…
-[Shizu laughs]

690
00:32:51,845 --> 00:32:53,805
-Oh man, you guys are killing it.
-Actually?

691
00:32:53,889 --> 00:32:56,224
You're moving around. Ready for the photo?

692
00:32:56,308 --> 00:32:57,309
Yep.

693
00:32:57,392 --> 00:33:00,687
You sure? Are you mentally prepared
for the trip to end?

694
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:02,564
Our adventure won't end here.

695
00:33:02,647 --> 00:33:04,024
Because, Machu…

696
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:05,525
Still on a journey.

697
00:33:05,609 --> 00:33:07,277
Whoo!

698
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:08,445
Let's go!

699
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:10,947
Hey, hey, hey!

700
00:33:17,746 --> 00:33:21,833
How do I put it… For some reason,
happy tears came out.

701
00:33:23,335 --> 00:33:25,170
Maybe it's…

702
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:31,343
because of the life lessons
I learned on this trip.

703
00:33:33,637 --> 00:33:38,850
That's right. It was such an invaluable
learning experience.

704
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:45,690
As a Travis Japan member,
there will be moments

705
00:33:46,233 --> 00:33:51,863
when the lessons I learned from this trip
will carry me forward.

706
00:33:52,530 --> 00:33:58,620
The last ten days were
so fulfilling and worthwhile.

707
00:33:58,703 --> 00:33:59,955
What can I say?

708
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:05,835
Now that I had this chance to expand
my knowledge on modern America…

709
00:34:05,919 --> 00:34:09,047
-Why don't you take a seat?
-I want to board the Amtrak. The Amtrak…

710
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:11,299
-You're so considerate. Thank you.
-Thanks.

711
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:13,718
-Oh, you don't wanna sit?
-Oh, I'm happy to oblige.

712
00:34:13,802 --> 00:34:16,096
-Thank you, I'll sit on the right half.
-You sure? Okay.

713
00:34:16,179 --> 00:34:18,807
Yes, it'd be great to ride
the Amtrak again.

714
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:23,061
Next time, I'd like to plan an Amtrak trip

715
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:25,981
with a completely different route.

716
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:28,066
Maybe I'll invite the members
for this one too,

717
00:34:28,149 --> 00:34:30,235
but we won't make plans to meet up.

718
00:34:30,318 --> 00:34:33,238
We'll see if we run into each other
at one of the stops.

719
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:36,533
It'd be fun to plan a trip
where everything is up to luck.

720
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:39,911
I was happy we ended our trip here.

721
00:34:39,995 --> 00:34:44,207
Try as we may to hold fast
to the dreams we started out with,

722
00:34:45,041 --> 00:34:47,168
as the days turn into months and years,

723
00:34:47,252 --> 00:34:51,256
we often find ourselves forgetting
what we once set out to do.

724
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:56,094
That's why we need to return to our roots.

725
00:34:56,845 --> 00:34:59,389
This trip gave me the chance
to return to my old dreams.

726
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:03,643
Now, I can continue onwards with
this renewed determination in my heart.

727
00:35:03,727 --> 00:35:07,981
I saw many aspects of Travis Japan's,

728
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:11,359
well, personality.

729
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:13,028
Really, I did.

730
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:17,741
It was filled with many happy moments.
We had a lot of them, and…

731
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:22,621
And when our memories
finally reach the fans, then…

732
00:35:22,704 --> 00:35:24,748
Oh my gosh, so happy.

733
00:35:25,332 --> 00:35:31,504
I want to continue making memories
with Travis Japan.

734
00:35:33,882 --> 00:35:34,924
I hope we do!

735
00:35:35,008 --> 00:35:38,595
I have some of the best memories
of my life thanks to this trip.

736
00:35:38,678 --> 00:35:40,305
I've also wised up a bit too.

737
00:35:40,388 --> 00:35:44,559
I had many firsts on this trip. I've never
hiked such a tall mountain before.

738
00:35:44,643 --> 00:35:48,188
It was also my first time visiting Arches.

739
00:35:48,271 --> 00:35:52,609
I didn't expect to encounter so much
wildlife either. We even saw jackrabbits.

740
00:35:52,692 --> 00:35:56,863
It was great to witness
the majestic landscapes

741
00:35:56,946 --> 00:35:58,823
after hiking with the band members.

742
00:35:59,407 --> 00:36:00,700
Let's see. Well…

743
00:36:02,619 --> 00:36:06,247
first and foremost…
it gave me appreciation for life.

744
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:10,835
This was my first trip
that truly felt like an adventure.

745
00:36:10,919 --> 00:36:11,920
Yeah.

746
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:14,339
Never before have I been
on a trip like this.

747
00:36:14,422 --> 00:36:18,843
Not only was it fun,
it left me with a thirst for adventures.

748
00:36:18,927 --> 00:36:20,261
Oh, really?

749
00:36:20,345 --> 00:36:22,514
-Yeah. I want to venture out…
-Will we go again?

750
00:36:22,597 --> 00:36:25,183
-…and see many new sights.
-You're gonna turn around?

751
00:36:26,059 --> 00:36:27,435
-Didn't you feel similarly?
-I did.

752
00:36:27,519 --> 00:36:30,814
In ten days alone, we visited
so many interesting places.

753
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:34,567
It reminded me that we can take off
with nothing but ourselves.

754
00:36:34,651 --> 00:36:37,946
It opened my eyes to the world.

755
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:39,906
-That's wonderful.
-Thanks.

756
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:42,367
What is it?
Stop turning around to look at me.

757
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:45,161
-What about you, Kaito?
-Me? Let's see.

758
00:36:45,245 --> 00:36:48,790
Next time, I want to visit France
and learn the background

759
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:50,709
-of my favorite brand.
-Right, right.

760
00:36:50,792 --> 00:36:54,796
Yes, I want to learn
the roots of my favorite fashion.

761
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:57,257
I want to go somewhere in France.

762
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:59,050
-What a nice idea.
-How's this?

763
00:36:59,759 --> 00:37:01,386
-I don't mind it.
-What?

764
00:37:02,554 --> 00:37:06,015
How fun… This trip taught me
how to enjoy traveling.

765
00:37:06,099 --> 00:37:09,060
-You're right. You're right.
-Now, the possibilities are endless.

766
00:37:09,144 --> 00:37:12,439
Travis Japan's adventure continues on.

767
00:37:13,773 --> 00:37:18,027
Can we keep moving forward with everyone?

768
00:37:18,111 --> 00:37:19,904
Agreed!

769
00:37:19,988 --> 00:37:21,906
[cheering]

770
00:37:25,076 --> 00:37:29,289
-Thanks, guys!
-It was the best trip ever!

771
00:37:36,212 --> 00:37:39,674
[Noel] We found our roots
in this summer vacation.

772
00:38:12,207 --> 00:38:14,209
Translated by Megumi Hunter
